{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_8863b59f0dc1450b8b3f5c9a","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"echo \"TALLY_BRIEF=$TALLY_BRIEF\"; cat \"$TALLY_BRIEF\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/676e182f5a7a6f83d12a8766e0ed09153857bdcb450c494819590bbf3d3cddb4.json\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task container-recipe: Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"container\\\",\\\"results/receipts\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:9d9cc2f4fab9a62b717733f670ebb391287c6f1e68dd2f0b6d9d54e79325fbd7\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"bash -n container/build.sh && grep -q 'torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'mecattaf/vllm' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'flashnext:dev' container/build.sh && grep -qi 'MIT' container/Containerfile\"],\"description\":\"The recipe pins the exact wheel set, the fork branch, and the image tag, and is syntax-clean.\",\"id\":\"recipe-pins\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"container\",\"results/receipts\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"A reproducible image build from the fork at the exactly pinned wheel set\",\"A build receipt the receipts gate can grade\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"THE PRIMARY ENGINE LANE of spec ruling P4 (the nix wiring in the tree is the graduation lane — leave it alone). Write container/Containerfile and container/build.sh implementing IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2 and spec claim 3.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3), designed for overnight iteration: the fork checkout and its build directory are bind-mounted volumes with ccache enabled so a one-line patch rebuild recompiles only what changed, and the image can be entered for edit-and-restart iteration without a rebuild. Containerfile: Ubuntu 24.04; python 3.12 venv at /opt/venv; install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and the matching triton wheel from the vendor stable index https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (record the exact resolved triton version); git clone --depth 1 --branch flashnext https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm and build it from source against those wheels for GPU target gfx1151 (relax nothing: the torch pin is satisfied exactly; drop audio extras rather than adding torchaudio); COPY container/rootfs/ into site-packages so the fn_ instrument modules land importable; write /opt/flashnext/build-info.json inside the image carrying the fork commit, torch, triton, and image build time. build.sh: run the packaging tests first, then podman build tagged flashnext:dev, then write results/receipts/build.json as {step:\\\"build\\\", status, ts, data:{torch, triton, fork_commit, image_digest}} with status fail on any error. Credit the recipe shape to the MIT toolbox recipe named in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the Containerfile header. Boundaries: touch only container/ and results/receipts/.\",\"id\":\"container-recipe\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3\",\"IMPORTS.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:6e8621b55de3a3a9c646edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361\",\"title\":\"Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"a428fee66b83d95682b418d5fdb4d975068e66ab\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-d4269a6f09b9/container-recipe\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"container\",\"results/receipts\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/container-recipe-6e8621b55de3a3a9\",\"taskId\":\"container-recipe\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/d4269a6f09b9/container-recipe\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER ADVISORY (arm-time): (1) A warm local wheel cache exists at /home/tom/.cache/flashnext-wheels/ on the coordinator with torch-2.13.0+rocm7.14.0, torchvision-0.28.0+rocm7.14.0, and triton-3.6.0+rocm7.14.0 cp312 linux_x86_64 wheels pre-downloaded from the vendor index. Your Containerfile must still reference https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (the acceptance grep requires it), but build.sh may bind-mount the cache dir and pass --find-links to pip so the multi-GB torch wheel is not re-downloaded at image build. (2) ubuntu:24.04 base image is already pulled locally via podman. (3) Do not add torchaudio — drop audio extras (the goal text is authoritative). (4) The build must ride ethernet (default route); never touch a 10.99.0.x address.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:09:35.472Z\",\"id\":2,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:09:35.472Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/2\"},{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER (post-failure insurance, applies to any future attempt): the previous attempt did all the work — authored container/, ran the full 64-minute build, wrote the receipt — then exited WITHOUT committing, and the driver failed it at ownership validation (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\"). Your final acts, in order, MUST be: (1) run the acceptance argv yourself and see it pass; (2) git add ONLY paths inside your conflict domains (container/, results/receipts/); (3) git commit with a descriptive message; (4) verify `git status --porcelain` is empty before you finish. Note the flashnext:dev image and its layers already exist in podman storage from the prior attempt — a re-run of build.sh should be fast via layer cache; do not prune or rebuild from scratch.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-29T07:11:19.614Z\",\"id\":4,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-29T07:11:19.614Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/4\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[4],\"preparedCommentIds\":[2],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":2,\"recheckedCursor\":4,\"registrationId\":\"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}"}],"details":{}}}
