flashnext:dev' container/build.sh && grep -qi 'MIT' container/Containerfile\"],\"description\":\"The recipe pins the exact wheel set, the fork branch, and the image tag, and is syntax-clean.\",\"id\":\"recipe-pins\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"container\",\"results/receipts\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"A reproducible image build from the fork at the exactly pinned wheel set\",\"A build receipt the receipts gate can grade\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"THE PRIMARY ENGINE LANE of spec ruling P4 (the nix wiring in the tree is the graduation lane — leave it alone). Write container/Containerfile and container/build.sh implementing IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2 and spec claim 3.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3), designed for overnight iteration: the fork checkout and its build directory are bind-mounted volumes with ccache enabled so a one-line patch rebuild recompiles only what changed, and the image can be entered for edit-and-restart iteration without a rebuild. Containerfile: Ubuntu 24.04; python 3.12 venv at /opt/venv; install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and the matching triton wheel from the vendor stable index https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (record the exact resolved triton version); git clone --depth 1 --branch flashnext https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm and build it from source against those wheels for GPU target gfx1151 (relax nothing: the torch pin is satisfied exactly; drop audio extras rather than adding torchaudio); COPY container/rootfs/ into site-packages so the fn_ instrument modules land importable; write /opt/flashnext/build-info.json inside the image carrying the fork commit, torch, triton, and image build time. build.sh: run the packaging tests first, then podman build tagged flashnext:dev, then write results/receipts/build.json as {step:\\\"build\\\", status, ts, data:{torch, triton, fork_commit, image_digest}} with status fail on any error. Credit the recipe shape to the MIT toolbox recipe named in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the Containerfile header. Boundaries: touch only container/ and results/receipts/.\",\"id\":\"container-recipe\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3\",\"IMPORTS.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:6e8621b55de3a3a9c646edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361\",\"title\":\"Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"a428fee66b83d95682b418d5fdb4d975068e66ab\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-d4269a6f09b9/container-recipe\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"container\",\"results/receipts\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/container-recipe-6e8621b55de3a3a9\",\"taskId\":\"container-recipe\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/d4269a6f09b9/container-recipe\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER ADVISORY (arm-time): (1) A warm local wheel cache exists at /home/tom/.cache/flashnext-wheels/ on the coordinator with torch-2.13.0+rocm7.14.0, torchvision-0.28.0+rocm7.14.0, and triton-3.6.0+rocm7.14.0 cp312 linux_x86_64 wheels pre-downloaded from the vendor index. Your Containerfile must still reference https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (the acceptance grep requires it), but build.sh may bind-mount the cache dir and pass --find-links to pip so the multi-GB torch wheel is not re-downloaded at image build. (2) ubuntu:24.04 base image is already pulled locally via podman. (3) Do not add torchaudio — drop audio extras (the goal text is authoritative). (4) The build must ride ethernet (default route); never touch a 10.99.0.x address.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:09:35.472Z\",\"id\":2,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:09:35.472Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/2\"